Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo1@paisafollows.test", "password": "password123" }

### 75. Create an alert on TRENT, so the rename has something to cascade into
POST http://localhost:8080/api/alerts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "TRENT", "direction": "BELOW", "targetPrice": 1 }

### 76. Symbol change (UPDATE with CASCADE): expect alertsFollowed >= 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/instruments/TRENT/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newSymbol": "TRENTLTD" }

### 77. The alert now shows TRENTLTD without any code touching it
GET http://localhost:8080/api/alerts

### 78. Rename it back
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/instruments/TRENTLTD/rename
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newSymbol": "TRENT" }

### 79. Delist (DELETE without cascade): expect deleted=false, status INACTIVE
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/admin/instruments/TRENT

### 80. Try to buy it: expect "TRENT is not tradable"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "TRENT", "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 1 }

### 81. Re-activate it
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/instruments/TRENT/activate

